    "question": {
      ":question/id": "dc5b583a-1cc5-57e6-ada3-1663f55e079d",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st and $4$th rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & 5 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st and $4$th rows of $A$ are $-5$ and $-8$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 0 & 5 & 9 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -8 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $-5+(-8)=-13.$",
